From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: vdec: hevc: an IDR or BLA picture releases every earlier reference

References are marked by POC alone, and every IDR has POC 0: the pictures
after an IDR reference the new one, and with it every earlier IDR still in
the list. Each IDR's CAPTURE buffer stayed referenced until a picture's set
no longer named POC 0; with GOPs that short, never. One buffer leaked per
IDR and the decode stalled once all were gone: 4K clips of three pictures
back to back gave 40 of 60 frames and never ended the stream.

An IDR or BLA picture leaves every earlier picture unused for reference,
as the specification has it.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 vdec/codec_hevc.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff -ruN a/vdec/codec_hevc.c b/vdec/codec_hevc.c
--- a/vdec/codec_hevc.c
+++ b/vdec/codec_hevc.c
@@ -671,6 +671,13 @@ static void codec_hevc_update_referenced(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 	union rpm_param *param = &hevc->rpm_param;
 	struct hevc_frame *frame;
 	u32 rps_used_bit = hevc->rps_used_bit;
+	u32 nal_unit_type = param->p.m_nalUnitType;
+	/* an IDR or BLA picture leaves every earlier picture unused for reference */
+	bool irap_reset = nal_unit_type == NAL_UNIT_CODED_SLICE_IDR ||
+			  nal_unit_type == NAL_UNIT_CODED_SLICE_IDR_N_LP ||
+			  nal_unit_type == NAL_UNIT_CODED_SLICE_BLA ||
+			  nal_unit_type == NAL_UNIT_CODED_SLICE_BLANT ||
+			  nal_unit_type == NAL_UNIT_CODED_SLICE_BLA_N_LP;
 	int i;
 	u32 curr_poc = hevc->curr_poc;
 
@@ -681,7 +688,7 @@ static void codec_hevc_update_referenced(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 		if (!frame->referenced)
 			continue;
 
-		for (i = 0; i < MAX_REF_ACTIVE; i++) {
+		for (i = 0; !irap_reset && i < MAX_REF_ACTIVE; i++) {
 			int delt;
 
 			if (param->p.CUR_RPS[i] & 0x8000)
-- 
